[1m[38;5;231mHow should user identity appear in log records?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mHashed / truncated id (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mLog a stable hash or truncated form. Still correlates a user's report to their sessions, but the log store holds no
[39m     [38;5;246mraw personal data.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Raw username
     [38;5;246mEasiest to read and grep, matches what app.js does today. Puts personal data in the collector and in every backup [39m
     [38;5;246mof it.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m No user identifier
     [38;5;246mMaximum privacy. You lose the ability to tie a reported problem to the sessions that caused it.[39m
